## Output policy

Product/backend output must be English for both direct Codex SDK/app-server and KAB-mediated backend lanes. In Stage 1 direct Codex work, use `templates/runners/direct-codex-sdk-appserver-runner.py.tmpl` (`openai_codex` -> `codex app-server --listen stdio://`) and record runner metadata, `thread_id`, prompt/output paths, and no-KAB-Codex rationale; do not use `codex exec`, generic `openai` SDK, raw app-server transport, or KAB `native_codex` evidence as Stage 1 proof. Console output must stay compact:

```text
Status: <pass|fail|blocked|in_progress|not_applicable>
Summary: <1-5 bullets>
Files: <changed/inspected paths only>
Verification: <commands/checks and short result>
Risks/blockers: <only actionable remaining issues>
Detailed artifact: <path or not_applicable reason>
Next action requested: <approval/review/none>
```

Detailed plans, logs, diffs, reviews, findings, and file excerpts belong in `.kkachi/runs/<run_id>/artifacts/<phase>/backend-<phase>.md` or the concrete phase artifact requested by KHS. Do not paste long plans, full diffs, full logs, full file contents, long reviews, or exhaustive checklist text into chat. If the detailed artifact cannot be written, report `Status: blocked` with the artifact-write blocker and do not dump the full detail into chat.

Continuity retrieval must be read-summary-first when compact artifacts exist: read `run-summary.yaml`, then the relevant `phase-packets/<phase>.yaml`, then targeted source artifact ranges only when checksums mismatch, status is fail/blocked, compression-forbidden evidence is needed, review/final-gate findings are blocking, or packet validity is stale/invalid/superseded. Compact packets and summaries are reversible indexes; they must preserve artifact paths, checksums, retrieval instructions, and invalidation behavior, and must not discard evidence, require Hermes proxy/headroom/runtime context pruning, give KAH subjective summarization authority, give KAB compression-policy authority, or authorize auth/token/provider/gateway/model mutation.

